# wordcount reads no environment variables and no configuration file.
#
# There is deliberately nothing to configure: the tool takes one FILE path on
# the command line and prints its word count. This file exists so that the
# "copy .env.example to .env" habit is a no-op rather than a mystery — every
# line here is a comment, and `cp .env.example .env` changes nothing about how
# wordcount runs.
#
# Do not add secrets here. wordcount has no server, no database and no network.
